From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: gate the N-PHY TSSIA setup on the radio rev, not the PHY rev

Both TSSIA writes in b43_nphy_ipa_internal_tssi_setup() sit inside a
dev->phy.rev >= 7 branch and are guarded by phy->rev != 5, which can
therefore never be false. brcmsmac guards them on pi->pubpi.radiorev != 5,
and radio 2057 is only reached from phy rev 7 upwards, so the two revisions
were transposed; b43 gets it right elsewhere, in b43_radio_2057_setup().

In the 5 GHz branch that also collapsed two nested conditions into one.
brcmsmac decides whether to write from the radio revision and which value
to write from the PHY revision, 0x31 on phy rev 7 and 0x1 otherwise, so as
written b43 can never produce 0x31 there.

Untested: this changes what a radio 2057 rev 5 board programs, and what a
phy rev 7 board programs in 5 GHz, and I have neither. It is just what the
brcmsmac driver does.


Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n17071
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n17089
Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -3857,7 +3857,7 @@
 			if (b43_current_band(dev->wl) == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ) {
 				b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0x5, 0x5);
 				b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0x9, 0xE);
-				if (phy->rev != 5)
+				if (phy->radio_rev != 5)
 					b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0xA, 0);
 				if (phy->rev != 7)
 					b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0xB, 1);
@@ -3867,10 +3867,13 @@
 				b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0x5, 0x9);
 				b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0x9, 0xC);
 				b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0xB, 0x0);
-				if (phy->rev != 5)
-					b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0xA, 1);
-				else
-					b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0xA, 0x31);
+				if (phy->radio_rev != 5) {
+					if (phy->rev != 7)
+						b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0xA, 1);
+					else
+						b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0xA,
+								0x31);
+				}
 			}
 			b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0x6, 0);
 			b43_radio_write(dev, r + 0x7, 0);
